{
  "comment": "The five activity clips tools/bodies/index.mjs writes into Woman, Farmer, Adventurer and King (#787, #788). One row per clip. `cycles` is how many times the motion repeats over the body's own Idle length, and it has to be an integer or the clip does not loop. `driver` is the joint test/assets.mjs check 7 holds to at least 20 degrees of motion away from Idle. Each move is { bone, axis, rest, amp, phase }: a glTF joint name, an axis in the body's model frame (+x the body's left, +y up, +z the way it faces), a static offset and an amplitude in degrees, and a phase in cycles. The angle at key k of 50 is rest + amp * sin(2 pi (cycles * k / 50 + phase)), composed onto Idle's pose at that key, root to tip. A positive angle about x tips +y towards +z: a lean forward for a spine joint, an arm swung back for a hanging arm. Negative about x brings a hanging arm forward and bends a forward forearm up. Positive about y turns to the body's left; positive about z carries a hanging hand to its left. Edit a row, run `npm run bodies:render`, commit the .glb with it.",
